Design: I propose to add simple test-time augmentation (horizontal flip) during validation and inference: for each image we predict on both the original and its horizontal flip, then average the sigmoid probabilities. This requires no extra training, slightly increases inference time, and often boosts AUROC by reducing prediction variance. We’ll integrate this into the cross‐validation loop to measure uplift and into the `predict` function. The rest of the training pipeline remains unchanged.
